# Cloudflare Pages headers of the Flutter PWA (Pages project te-tengo-app: production
# https://app.tetengo.reqsai.tech, staging https://staging.te-tengo-app.pages.dev). The reusable
# build-web.yml copies this folder into the Flutter build output (build/web), so the artifact that
# release.yml deploys already contains it. Flutter and Firebase need their own policy, so the
# landing's CSP, COOP and Permissions-Policy are not applied here.
# File names are not hashed and the app's own service worker (firebase-messaging-sw.js, scope /)
# caches network first, so everything revalidates.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# Flutter's deprecated worker is emitted but never registered (docs/WEB_PWA.md); never let a browser
# keep a stale copy.
/flutter_service_worker.js
  Cache-Control: no-store
